        "sections": [
          {
            "section_type": "example_question",
            "normalized_html": "<p>Given that <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac 3 {2x}=a]</span> and <span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\dfrac y x=b,]</span> what is <span class=\"math\">[MATH: a+b?]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "Given that [MATH: \\dfrac 3 {2x}=a] and [MATH: \\dfrac y x=b,] what is [MATH: a+b?]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "content",
            "normalized_html": "<p>EXPLANATION</p>",
            "readable_text": "EXPLANATION",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          },
          {
            "section_type": "example_explanation",
            "normalized_html": "<p>We wish to add the following fractions:\n<span class=\"math\">[MATH: a+b = \\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x]</span></p><p>In order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2x]</span> if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by <span class=\"math\">[MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]</span></p><p><span class=\"math\">[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x &amp;= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac 2 2 \\cdot \\dfrac y x &amp;= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac {2y} {2x} &amp;= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac {3 + 2y} {2x}\n}]</span></p>",
            "readable_text": "We wish to add the following fractions:\n[MATH: a+b = \\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x]\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of [MATH: 2x] if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by [MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac 2 2 \\cdot \\dfrac y x &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac {2y} {2x} &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac {3 + 2y} {2x}\n}]",
            "images": [],
            "free_entry_blanks": [],
            "select_lists": []
          }
        ],
        "images": [],
        "free_entry_blanks": [],
        "select_lists": [],
        "readable_text": "Example Prompt:\nGiven that [MATH: \\dfrac 3 {2x}=a] and [MATH: \\dfrac y x=b,] what is [MATH: a+b?]\n\nContent:\nEXPLANATION\n\nExplanation:\nWe wish to add the following fractions:\n[MATH: a+b = \\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x]\n\nIn order to add the two fractions, we need them to have a common denominator. Here, we can put both fractions over a common denominator of [MATH: 2x] if we multiply the top and bottom of the second fraction by [MATH: 2\\mathbin{:}]\n\n[MATH: \\eqalign{\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac y x &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac 2 2 \\cdot \\dfrac y x &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac 3 {2x} + \\dfrac {2y} {2x} &= \\[5pt]\n\\dfrac {3 + 2y} {2x}\n}]"
      },
